#51: 
 casting value returned by memory allocation function to (struct octeon_dispatch *) is useless.

CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer vmalloc(sizeof(*dispatch)...) over vmalloc(sizeof(struct octeon_dispatch)...)
#68: FILE: drivers/net/ethernet/cavium/liquidio/octeon_device.c:1155:
+		dispatch = vmalloc(sizeof(struct octeon_dispatch));

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

